    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202-a8">

                <pb facs="0359" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg247"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to Consul-General
                    Bergholz</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-10-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my No. 1374 of August 16
                    last, and replying to your No. 127 of August 21, 1907, I inclose herewith a note
                    from the Wai-wu Pu, dated the 8th instant, which is self-explanatory and which
                    settles the matter of equality of treatment of goods reexported from Hongkong
                    and Canton to West River ports.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                    Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
